research/audit/wave3-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:38:{"id":"thm-young-inequality","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf","https://e.math.cornell.edu/people/belk/measuretheory/Inequalities.pdf","https://math.oregonstate.edu/~show/old/142_Luenberger.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter, Cornell, and Oregon State give Young, Hölder, and Minkowski for finite sums with the standard normalization and Hölder-based arguments semantically matching “Young's inequality for products (rational conjugate exponents)”. The item specializes the established inequality to finite lists and makes its zero, empty-list, rational-exponent, and equality boundaries explicit. Its numbered proof is an expanded, dependency-explicit reconstruction of the standard weighted-AM–GM derivation, so it is recoverable established mathematics rather than a positive novelty determination. The local wording and, where present, proof decomposition are not exact-source matches, so each supplied component is conservatively classified as shown; no component is labeled ai-generated merely because an exact transcription did not surface. URL verification route: model-side web open returned content for every recorded URL on 2026-08-04 (HTTP 200); shell DNS was not used.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
