---
id: ex-the-metric-urysohn-function-costs-no-choice
kind: example
title: "In a metric space the function $d(x,A)/(d(x,A) + d(x,B))$ separates two disjoint closed sets outright, so the metric case spends no choice principle"
status: published
origin: session
provenance:
